\(\(as const \(Array \(_ BitVec (32|64)\) \(_ BitVec 8\)\)\) \(_ bv0 8\)\)
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
\(\(as const \(Array \(_ BitVec (32|64)\) \(_ BitVec 8\)\)\) \(\(_ extract
--
cvc5 accepts `((as const (Array I E)) v)' only for a VALUE v ("invalid
argument ... expected a value").  Turning the bit-vector of the union s.u
back into an array (unflatten) used the array's element 0 -- an extract of
a term -- as the default value; for cvc5 the default is now zero and all
elements are stored.  `cbmc --cvc5' on this program verifies (it reported a
parse error).  broken-smt-backend: the test inspects the output only.
